--- Overview
Adds Located.ExpandMapping to cmdconfig. It returns the variable-expansion mapping that Load and LoadFiles use, so callers can add defaults or record unresolved variables. LoadFiles now uses this method instead of building the mapping inline.

--- Key Changes
  * cmdutil/cmdconfig
    * New (*Located).ExpandMapping(then ...func(string) string) (func(string) string, error):
      * Merges the env files in l.Env.
      * Resolves variables from the process environment first, then from those files (envfile.ExpandingMapping).
      * Chains any extra then mappings after that using envfile.ChainMapping, for example envfile.DefaultsMapping or envfile.Unresolved.Mapping.
    * LoadFiles now gets its default mapping from loc.ExpandMapping(). Behavior and error wrapping (read environment variables from <file>: ...) are the same as before.
    * The README documents the new method with an example: pass the result to LoadFiles via cmdyaml.WithExpandMapping, together with cmdyaml.WithUnresolvedEmpty().
  * Tests
    * New TestLocatedExpandMapping. It checks that values are resolved in order (process env, then env file, then defaults), that unresolved names are recorded, and that a missing env file produces an error.

